From ad9c0be185847b19d8e69374410cf445c1c340ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:47:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] hal: the Stage dispatches through this file's table on
 the 3DS

On the PC the Stage ctor's last store installs hal/stage_bridges.cpp's
_ZTV5Stage, which hal_fill_stage_vtable fills (slot 0 the host boot body
st_init, the ROM's own bodies elsewhere). The 3DS build compiles Stage's key
function from src/, so GCC emits the class's real table and the ctor installs
that: slot 0 became the ROM's Stage::InitResources, the route this file does
not run. Under SM64DS_HOST_3DS port_stage_create points the Stage at this
file's table, as on the PC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 port/hal/stage_bridges.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/port/hal/stage_bridges.cpp b/port/hal/stage_bridges.cpp
index bb3b54cb4..a57c2e71e 100644
--- a/port/hal/stage_bridges.cpp
+++ b/port/hal/stage_bridges.cpp
@@ -1234,6 +1234,17 @@ extern "C" void *port_stage_create(void)
         std::fprintf(stderr, "FATAL: Stage::Stage returned null\n");
         std::abort();
     }
+#if defined(SM64DS_HOST_3DS)
+    /* THE TABLE THE STAGE DISPATCHES THROUGH. On the PC the ctor's last store
+       installs this file's _ZTV5Stage, the table hal_fill_stage_vtable just
+       filled (slot 0 the boot body, the ROM's own bodies in the rest). The 3DS
+       build compiles Stage's key function from src/, so GCC emits the class's
+       real table and the ctor installs THAT one: slot 0 would be the ROM's
+       Stage::InitResources, which this file does not run (see the lifecycle
+       seat below). Point the Stage at this file's table, as on the PC. ROM
+       slot n is element n here and Itanium slot n in GCC's dispatch alike. */
+    *(void ***)g_stage = _ZTV5Stage;
+#endif
 
     /* The tree head, asserted rather than assumed. The Stage is built with
        data_020a4b6c[0] still null, so func_0203b438 takes its no-parent branch
-- 
